menu "Smart-Air AI Scheduler"

    config SA_AI_ENABLED
        bool "Enable on-device AI inference + auto Fan control"
        default n
        help
            Strictly opt-in for the first hardware bring-up (see
            ai/README.md). When disabled, ai_scheduler_start() is a no-op:
            no task is created, no relay/buzzer/MQTT calls are ever made --
            firmware behaves exactly as it did before this feature existed.

    config SA_AI_FAN_RELAY_CHANNEL
        int "Relay channel the AI controls (1-based)"
        depends on SA_AI_ENABLED
        default 1
        range 1 3
        help
            Per the app's own channel labeling (relay_1=Fan, relay_2=Lamp,
            relay_3=Filter -- see app/lib/screens/devices/
            device_dashboard_screen.dart), the AI should control the Fan
            channel (default 1). Only ONE channel is ever touched by AI.

    config SA_AI_OVERRIDE_COOLDOWN_MIN
        int "Minutes to back off after an external relay change (minutes)"
        depends on SA_AI_ENABLED
        default 30
        range 1 240
        help
            Whenever the AI-controlled relay's actual state no longer
            matches what the AI last commanded (detected by polling
            relay_get(), no changes to relay.c/mqtt.c needed), the AI
            scheduler assumes a human (app tap) or another controller (the
            existing server/ai-service, if its own auto_mode is still on)
            just took over, and stays hands-off on that channel for this
            many minutes before resuming automatic control.

endmenu
